---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import hubs from '../../context/data/hubs.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const { themes, gaps } = hubs;
---

<Base
  title="Hub cards"
  description="A worked example of hub cards — what to do when your interests cut across a numbering scheme, which they always will."
  derived
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Worked example</p>
    <h1>Hub cards</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Six standing interests, mapped onto the numbering. None of them fit in one division —
      which is the normal case, not the awkward one, and exactly what a hub card exists to fix.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      A hub is the one card you are allowed to rewrite, because it holds no thinking — only
      addresses. That licence is what lets it collapse the drawer separation the four-digit
      numbers impose. <a href={`${base}/rules`}>The three index devices →</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The six hubs</h2>
  <div class="strip">
    {
      themes.map((t) => (
        <a href={`#${t.name.toLowerCase()}`}>
          <span class="ad">{t.hub}</span>
          <span class="nm">{t.name}</span>
          <span class="bh">
            behind <span class="ad">{t.anchor}</span> · {t.anchorTitle}
          </span>
        </a>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <p class="note-line">
    Each hub sits at its theme’s centre of gravity — the anchor most of its material hangs off
    — not at a drawer root. A drawer root is free and legal, and still wrong: a card there has
    hundreds of unrelated disciplines as neighbours, and neighbours are the point.
  </p>

  {
    themes.map((t) => (
      <section class="th" id={t.name.toLowerCase()}>
        <h2>{t.name}</h2>
        <div class="anchor">
          <span class="eyebrow">Hub card</span>
          <b class="ad">{t.hub}</b>
          <span class="eyebrow">behind</span>
          <b class="ad">{t.anchor}</b>
          <span class="at">{t.anchorTitle}</span>
        </div>
        <p class="why">{t.why}</p>
        {t.groups.map((g) => (
          <div class="grp">
            <h4 class="eyebrow">{g.name}</h4>
            <ul>
              {g.items.map((i) => (
                <li>
                  <span class="ad">{i.address}</span>
                  <span>{i.title}</span>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))}
      </section>
    ))
  }

  <h2>When your vocabulary is not in the map</h2>
  <p>
    Of 23 terms probed from these six themes, <strong>22 have no entry in the source outline at
    all.</strong> Sales, startups, keto, productivity, attention, habit, negotiation, branding —
    none of them appear. Only “storytelling” does.
  </p>
  <div class="tbl">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Theme</th><th>Absent from the outline</th><th>File behind</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          gaps.map((g) => (
            <tr>
              <td><strong>{g.theme}</strong></td>
              <td class="absent">{g.absent}</td>
              <td class="ad">{g.fileBehind}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      This is not a defect in the map. An outline of academic disciplines records how
      universities partition inquiry. Your interests are mostly <em>practices</em> — things
      people do, sell, cook, and pray. There is no chair of keto.
    </p>
    <p>
      So expect your Antinet to invert the reference. The numbered entries are a
      <strong>skeleton of anchors</strong>, not a catalogue to complete. The overwhelming
      majority of your cards will be your own thinking branching off an anchor. A card on
      carnivore adaptation is not a missing discipline; it is a descendant of
      <span class="ad">5100/21a</span>, and it will sit among siblings no encyclopedia imagined.
    </p>
    <p>
      Which is the argument for keeping the keyword index sparse and the hub cards fat: the
      numbers cannot find your material, because your material is not what was numbered.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 3.5rem 0 0;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .strip {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--rule);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 3px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }
  .strip a {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.2rem 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .strip a:hover {
    background: var(--tint);
  }
  .strip .ad {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    flex: 0 0 6rem;
  }
  .strip .nm {
    font: 600 0.97rem var(--serif);
    flex: 0 0 9rem;
  }
  .strip .bh {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .strip .bh .ad {
    flex: none;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .note-line {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.89rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .th h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .anchor {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.2rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    margin: 0.9rem 0 1rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem;
    background: var(--tint);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--brass);
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .anchor b {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }
  .anchor .at {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .why {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.3rem;
  }
  .grp {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .grp h4 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .grp ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(18rem, 1fr));
    gap: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
  }
  .grp li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 0.12rem 0;
    font-size: 0.89rem;
    max-width: none;
  }
  .grp .ad {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--brass-dim);
    flex: 0 0 5rem;
  }
  .absent {
    color: var(--warn);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .grp li {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0 0.7rem;
    }
    .grp .ad {
      flex-basis: 100%;
    }
  }
</style>
